{title: 486 - I Do Believe}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #486 • }
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: F}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 486}
{meta: category Christian Life - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[F]Fa[C]ther, I [C7]stretch my [F]hands to Thee;
No [C]other [Bb]help I [F]know;
If [C7]Thou withdraw Thy[F]self from me,
Ah, [Bb]wither [Gm]shall [C7]I[F]go?
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[F]On [C]Thy dear [C7]Son I [F]now believe,
[C]O let [Bb]me feel [F]Thy power;
[C7]And all my [F]varied wants relieve,
[Bb]In [Gm]this [C7]accepted [F]hour.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[F]Author [C]of faith! [C7]To Thee [F]I lift
[C]My [Bb]weary, [F]longing eyes;
[C7]O let me [F]now receive that gift;
[Bb]My [Gm]soul [C7]without [F]it dies.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[F]Surely [C]Thou canst [C7]not let [F]me die;
[C]O speak, [Bb]and I [F]shall live;
[C7]And here I [F]will unwearied lie,
[Bb]Till [Gm]Thou [C7]Thy [F]Spirit give.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 5}
[F]How [C]would my [C7]fainting [F]soul rejoice
[C]Could I [Bb]but see [F]Thy face!
[C7]Now let me [F]hear Thy quickening voice,
[Bb]And [Gm]taste [C7]Thy [F]pardoning grace.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 6}
[F]I [C]do believe, [C7]I [F]now believe
[C]That [Bb]Jesus died [F]for me,
[C7]And that He [F]shed His precious blood
[Bb]From [Gm]sin to [C7]set [F]me free.
{end_of_verse}
